    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16518" root="ركض" body-key="r">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مِرْكَضَةٌ</span></b>  (tropical:)  A mare <i>that beats the ground with
her legs</i> (K, TA) <i>when she runs.</i> (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  See
also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَكُوضٌ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  Also (tropical:)  <i>A certain part of a bow;
well known; one of</i> [<i>the two parts called</i>] <i>its</i>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مِرْكَضَتَانِ</span>; (S;) or ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مِرْكَضَانِ</span></b> : (IB:) <i>each of
the two curved extremities thereof;</i> as also
↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مِرْكَضٌ</span></b> : (A:) or the <i>side thereof:</i> (K:) pl.
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَرَاكِضُ</span>. (TA.)

